codex
The rule audit found no result-fabricating or false rule on the proved integer-list executions, and the fresh false-result mutation built successfully but stopped on the correct computed result. The decisive issue is adequacy: the prompt’s contract accepts ordinary comparable lists without an integer element restriction, while every formal entry is confined to `VList(Ints)`; string and float witnesses execute correctly in both Python implementations but are not expressible by the theorem. Under the benchmark’s explicit mapping, that material domain narrowing requires `FAIL / NOT_LEGIT`.
The rule inventory and non-vacuity gates pass for finite integer lists, but the formal domain materially narrows the unrestricted comparable-list source contract, which the benchmark mandates mapping to FAIL / NOT_LEGIT.
